On Tue, 4 Sep 2001, Joseph Sirucka wrote:
> I have alphastation 400/233 with a raycom isa pcmcia card and a wavelan
> bronze wirless card. When the wireless card configures it finds the
> wireless card and a address space, but can't attach due not being able
> to have mac address.

I have a D-Link DWL-650, but is what you're seeing something like this?

wi0 at pcmcia0 function 0: D, Link DWL-650 11Mbps WLAN Card, Version 01.02,
 port 0x400-0x43fwi0: init failed
wi0: could not get mac address, attach failed

At first, I was thinking it was a problem with the wi driver, but then I
tried putting the card into my laptop's cardbus slot, and it worked
fine. I get the "could not get mac address" error with the Raycom PCMCIA
adapter in both NetBSD/i386 and NetBSD/alpha. However, if I boot the
i386 into Windows NT 4.0, the card works fine. So... it's something
about NetBSD, but I haven't been able to figure out what :(

What I've noticed is that when the wi driver reads from the card's I/O
space, it's always getting 8. With a patch Peter Seebach posted a couple
months back, I got:

wi0: too many bytes [8, expected 2] reading type 0xFCE0
wi0: too many bytes [8, expected 4] reading type 0xFC01
wi0: could not get mac address, attach failed

I tried adding more debug info, and no matter what the driver tried to
read, it was seeing an 8.
