I think you misunderstood something.
There are 3 Jumpers on the Drive (possibly marked with 0, 1 and 2), but
with these jumpers you jumper the bits 1, 2 and 4 - so if the jumper is on
position 2, your ID is 4. If you want to have ID 5, jumper it on 0 and 2
and so on...

